  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not pick a social science career track from "NGO or UPSC" alone. The label that sounds most
    respectable at a family gathering is not the one with the strongest growth curve, and the
    two-stage competition inside academia and government welfare recruitment rarely gets explained
    honestly before someone commits years to either.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      Pick the track using The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above — your energy, your real runway, current
      market demand, and AI exposure — not just which title sounds most respectable today.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then pass The 3 Gates on one small, real test before you commit a NET-JRF attempt, a PhD, or
      an unpaid internship season to it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Reaching earlier financial freedom from any of these seven tracks comes down to a genuine
    <strong>high-income skill portfolio</strong> — research method, data literacy, writing, and
    field judgment — built deliberately and proven publicly, not the social science label by itself.
    Move toward that with
